# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML portfolio site.

## Changes Made

### Created Files:
1. **package.json** - Added npm package configuration with @vercel/analytics dependency
   - Set up as ES module with basic metadata
   - Includes @vercel/analytics@^2.0.1 as a dependency

2. **package-lock.json** - Lockfile generated by npm to ensure consistent dependency versions

3. **.gitignore** - Added to exclude node_modules and build artifacts from version control

### Modified Files:
1. **index.html** - Added Vercel Web Analytics tracking scripts
   - Added the inline script to initialize the `window.va` function queue
   - Added deferred script tag to load `/_vercel/insights/script.js`
   - Scripts placed at the end of the body, just after the existing JavaScript includes

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation for plain HTML/Vanilla JS sites, I used the script tag approach which is the recommended method for static sites without a build process:

```html
<script>
  window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

This implementation:
- Initializes a queue for analytics events before the script loads
- Uses the Vercel-provided script path that will be automatically available when deployed on Vercel
- Loads the script with `defer` to avoid blocking page rendering
- Preserves all existing functionality and code structure

## Package Installation

- Installed @vercel/analytics package via npm
- Package version: 2.0.1 (latest stable version as of implementation)
- Lock file created to ensure consistent dependency resolution

## Verification

✅ Build process completes successfully (static site requires no build)
✅ Analytics scripts correctly added to index.html before closing body tag
✅ Package and lock files properly created
✅ .gitignore configured to exclude node_modules
✅ All changes staged for commit

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, the analytics will automatically start tracking:
- Page views
- User sessions
- Navigation patterns

You can verify the setup is working by:
1. Deploying the site to Vercel
2. Visiting the site and checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/`
3. Viewing analytics data in your Vercel dashboard under the project's Analytics tab

No additional configuration is required - the analytics will work automatically on Vercel's platform.
